<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karanga</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Karanga people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Karanga are a Shona-speaking people of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a>, the largest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shona">Shona</a> subgroups. Their ancestors are associated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-zimbabwe">Great Zimbabwe</a> and with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi</a> states, and several South African ruling lines, including those of the Lobedu and the Venda, trace their origins to Karanga country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karanga.jpg" alt="Karanga" width="320" height="467" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Hillewaert · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shona_witch_doctor_(Zimbabwe).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
